  "id": "dysregulation",
  "term": "dysregulation",
  "definition": "Dysregulation is a disturbance in the normal control of a body or brain system, such as the stress-response and neuroendocrine pathways. In this context, it is linked to problems with memory, executive functioning, and emotional regulation, and may contribute directly to worsening brain function by disrupting important neural circuits.",
